      "writtenOn": "2024-05-22T10:19:53Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "My understanding was that this was used for populating `VkAndroidHardwareBufferPropertiesANDROID` via `vkGetAndroidHardwareBufferPropertiesANDROID()`.\n\nThen, applications in the guest take the `format` and put it in the `VkImageCreateInfo` and take the `externalFormat` and put it in the `VkExternalFormatANDROID` (which is chained to the `VkImageCreateInfo::pNext`) for use with `vkCreateImage()`.\n\nIIUC, the `VkExternalFormatANDROID`/`externalFormat` is only used within the guest and is never sent to the host. A quick search for `VkExternalFormatANDROID` in `hardware/google/gfxstream/host` seems to confirm this which means old-guest plus new-host should be okay.",
      "parentUuid": "a6b10acf_1a762d38",
      "revId": "3eaf77cde099ec52f2f8caeae8511df9c57bf29e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
